Z4YVVBWFKr2g4", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "payments-worker", "version": "v3.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_017h6ADMAndhp7YsooUGcSF3", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "payments-worker errors after v3.4.0 deploy; rolled back to v3.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "payments-worker", "summary": "This morning's deploy of payments-worker v3.4.0 left the service unhealthy in all regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west), with an 18% error rate. Rolled back to v3.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production; the rollout is verified in all regions. Note: payments-api v5.1.0 is also showing as unhealthy/degraded (18% error rate). An approver turned down rolling it back and said the problem is in payments-worker. Check whether payments-api recovers now that the worker is rolled back.", "idempotency_key": "payments-worker-v3.4.0-rollback-sev2"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01J7cgd3itP4PM9cqDidtUeH", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "payments-worker"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01QLH8Bq9yADZkxty3ZMi7CS", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "payments-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I rolled payments-worker back to its last healthy release and opened the SEV2 incident. payments-worker has recovered, but payments-api is still unhealthy.\n\n**What happened:**\n- There's no service named \"payments.\" I found two candidates, payments-api and payments-worker, and both were unhealthy with an 18% error rate.\n- I first tried rolling back payments-api (v5.1.0 \u2192 v5.0.0). The approver denied it and said the problem is in payments-worker, so payments-api was not changed.\n- I rolled payments-worker back from v3.4.0, which was marked unhealthy, to **v3.3.0**, its most recent release that was healthy in production. It's now on v3.3.0 in us-east, us-west and eu-west, reports healthy, and its error rate is down to 0.2%.\n- I opened **INC-0001 (SEV2)** for payments-worker, and the on-call engineer has been paged. The incident also notes the payments-api issue.\n\n**Still open:** payments-api v5.1.0 is still unhealthy with an 18% error rate after the worker rollback. Since the approver turned down the payments-api rollback, I've left it alone. Someone should look into it separately, possibly through INC-0001.", "type": "text"}]}]}